tasks.description:
Fixes BUG-20. Every surface of /audit:status reads an in-flight phase from the copy that holds it live: the READY NOW list, the phase table, the progress counts, the --short entry view and the --json payload. All of them use the one reader the UNFINISHED block uses, reached through audit-status.py, while _status_facts stays pure. Every row read from a copy other than this checkout's own says which copy it was. When the live copy cannot be read, the row says it shows this checkout's copy and that this may not be current.

Cases, each with its twin:
- a phase in a linked worktree with tasks done there is not listed as ready, and is counted as done;
- a phase with no branch is read from this checkout;
- an unreadable worktree falls back with the stale wording;
- --short and --json agree with the full view.

Fixes review findings P115-R1 to P115-R4 and P115-R6. Every phase that is being worked on elsewhere is read live. The gate, the bug counts and RESUMABLE read this checkout, because they certify or advise about it.

- A phase is in flight when its lock exists, or when one git worktree list shows its branch checked out in a linked worktree and that branch is not merged into this checkout's HEAD. Both kinds go through the live reader. If a branch exists with no worktree and no lock, its row says so: the branch exists and was not read.
- --gate evaluates every condition over this checkout's own rollup. The overlay stays for the human render and --json. The main() comment and status.md's Gate mode section say which copy the gate reads.
- Bug status comes from this checkout. When a live copy shows a bug's fix elsewhere, the BUGS block and --json name that copy beside the bug.
- RESUMABLE reads this checkout and skips a phase whose lock is held live. status.md stays true.
- The lock directory is looked up once per invocation.

Cases, each with a twin:
- a lock-less phase done in its linked worktree is not ready, and its row names the worktree file;
- a lock-less phase with no branch is unchanged;
- a gate whose bug fix exists only in a worktree still fails open-bugs;
- a bug whose fix is shown elsewhere names the copy;
- a live-locked phase that is in progress in its worktree prints no RESUMABLE line on the development branch.
